course: dictionary
lesson: 3708
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Fleece can name a sheep's woolly coat, or a warm jacket. «Plastic bottles can be melted and spun into fibres for fleece jackets» is about clothes, because the word jackets comes right after it.
explain: The clues are the words around the word. «Most farm sheep grow wool that never stops, so they must be shorn» is about farms, so fleece means the coat of a sheep. Always ask: what is this sentence about? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Fleece can also be an informal verb meaning to cheat someone out of money. If a sentence is about prices, paying, or someone being tricked, that is the meaning to pick. When you are unsure, look the word up in a dictionary.
fact: Fleece means the woolly coat of a sheep, or the wool cut from one sheep in one piece.
fact: A fleece can also be a soft, warm jacket or jumper made of fluffy man-made fabric.
fact: To fleece someone (informal) means to cheat them out of money, often by charging far too much.
fact: «Plastic bottles can be melted and spun into fibres for fleece jackets.»
fact: In 2015 a runaway sheep in Australia named Chris was found with a fleece weighing about 40 kilograms.
exercise: «In 2015 a runaway sheep in Australia named Chris was found with a fleece weighing about 40 kilograms.» What is the fleece in this sentence? | A warm jacket for school trips | A bottle melted into fibres | A cheat | *The woolly coat of a sheep
exercise: «Plastic bottles can be melted and spun into fibres for fleece jackets.» What kind of thing is a fleece jacket? | *A soft, warm jacket made of fluffy man-made fabric | A sheep that has been shorn | A farm gate | A bottle that has been melted
exercise: Ella says, «The shop fleeced me, charging ten pounds for one pencil.» What does fleeced mean here? | Kept warm on a cold day | Cut like wool from a sheep | Given a free present | *Cheated out of money by charging far too much
test: «A heavy sheep with a thick fleece can roll onto its back and be unable to get up.» What is the fleece in this sentence? | *The sheep's woolly coat | A soft jacket for the farmer | A heavy rock | Thick grass
test: «Don't let that market stall fleece you; the price is far too high.» What does fleece mean in this sentence? | To cut wool from a sheep | *To cheat someone out of money | To keep someone warm | To wrap someone in a jacket
exam: «The school trip was cold, so Maya zipped up her fleece tight against the wind.» What does fleece mean here? | To cheat someone out of money | *A soft, warm jacket | A bottle melted into fibres | A sheep's woolly coat
